course: dictionary
lesson: 15935
title: Unrestrained
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unrestrained means not held back or controlled. The word is built from un- (not) and restrain (to hold back), so unrestrained means not held back. Think of a dog that is not on a lead: it is unrestrained.
explain: In stories, unrestrained is used for big feelings. «The crowd let out unrestrained cheers when the goal went in.» The cheers were loud and free, with nobody holding them back.
explain: In safety, unrestrained means not held in place. «A child who is unrestrained in a car can be badly hurt in a crash.» A car seat or seat belt is what restrains a child, so without one, the child is unrestrained.
fact: Unrestrained means not held back or controlled.
fact: The prefix un- means not, and restrain means to hold back.
fact: «Unrestrained joy» means joy that is free and not held back.
fact: «An unrestrained passenger» means a passenger who is not held in by a seat belt or a seat.
fact: «Unrestrained» can also describe a feeling, such as anger or laughter, that is not kept under control.
exercise: «When the team scored, the fans let out unrestrained cheers.» What does unrestrained mean here? | Tied up with rope | Held back, quiet and polite | Very tired | *Free and wild, not held back
exercise: «The dog ran into the road because it was unrestrained.» What does unrestrained mean in this sentence? | Very old | *Not held back or tied up | Wearing a collar with a name tag | Sleeping soundly
exercise: «The children shouted with unrestrained glee.» Copy the word that tells you the glee was not held back. | glee | children | shouted | *unrestrained
test: «An unrestrained passenger in a car can be badly hurt in a crash.» What does unrestrained passenger mean? | A passenger who is sleeping | A passenger wearing a seat belt | *A passenger not held in by a seat belt or seat | A passenger who is very tall
test: «She laughed unrestrainedly at the funny film.» What does unrestrainedly mean here? | Quietly and politely | Slowly, one step at a time | *Freely, without holding back | Sadly, with tears
exam: Which is the best meaning of «unrestrained joy»? | Joy that is held back and kept quiet | *Joy that is free and wild, not held back | Joy that is sad and tired | Joy that is shared with nobody
